Weather check logic (core):

```java
private record WeatherCheck(Long forecastVersion, Long standardsVersion,
                            String snapshotJson, List<WeatherViolationDto> violations) {}

private WeatherCheck checkWeather(Long forecastVersion, List<ZonePo> hitZones, List<Point> points) {
    // caller ensures coord_lock held
    long currentForecast = weatherRepo.getForecastVersion();
    if (!forecastVersion.equals(currentForecast)) → 409 VERSION_CONFLICT
    long standardsVersion = weatherRepo.getStandardsVersion();
    List<WeatherViolationDto> violations = new ArrayList<>();
    List<ObjectNode> snapshotZones = ...;
    for (ZonePo zone : hitZones) {  // zones path passes through
        List<WeatherMinimaPo> minima = weatherRepo.findMinima(zone.zoneId());
        if (minima.isEmpty()) continue;
        List<WeatherForecastPo> forecasts = weatherRepo.findForecastForZone(forecastVersion, zone.zoneId());
        for (WeatherMinimaPo m : minima) {
            // coverage check: union of forecast windows must cover [m.from, m.to)
            // find overlapping forecasts sorted by validFrom
            List<WeatherForecastPo> overlapping = forecasts overlapping [from,to);
            long cursor = m.effectiveFrom();
            for (f : overlapping sorted by validFrom) {
                if (f.validFrom() > cursor) → missing coverage [cursor, min(f.validFrom, to))
                // check values
                if (f.visibilityM < m.minVisibilityM) violation(VISIBILITY)
                if (f.cloudBaseM < m.minCloudBaseM) violation(CLOUD_BASE)
                cursor = max(cursor, f.validTo);
                if (cursor >= m.effectiveTo) break;
            }
            if (cursor < m.effectiveTo) → 422 FORECAST_MISSING with zoneId, window, missingFrom=cursor, missingTo
        }
    }
}
```

Wait — but hitZones for weather: zones the path passes through. Geometric hits = zones intersecting path. Weather check applies to those same zones. If a zone has minima and path passes through, forecast must exist → else 422. Even if zone would BLOCK anyway. OK.

Violation per (zone, minima window, metric) — if multiple forecast entries overlap the same window and violate, take the worst (min actual)? Or one violation per forecast entry? Simpler: one violation per (zone, window, metric) using the minimum actual value across overlapping entries. That gives stable output. Let me compute per window: minVisibility across overlapping entries; if < required → violation with actual=min.

Coverage gap → 422 with details: message includes zoneId and missing interval. Also response should include actual/required? For 422 error we only have code+message. Fine — message carries details.

Snapshot JSON: {"standardsVersion":N, "forecastVersion":M, "zones":[{zoneId, minima:[{from,to,minVisibility,minCloudBase}], forecasts:[{from,to,visibility,cloudBase}]}]}. Store via objectMapper.

Conclusion: violations non-empty → WEATHER_BLOCKED; else hits non-empty → BLOCKED; else CLEAR.

hitZoneIds in result: geometric hits (all zones path crosses). For WEATHER_BLOCKED, hitZoneIds still lists geometric hits? Hmm. Previously hitZoneIds = BLOCKED hits. For WEATHER_BLOCKED, I'll keep hitZoneIds = geometric hit zones (path crosses them) and weatherViolations separate. Document it.

Batch review: for each item, do the same as single review but collect ReviewPo; validate all first, then insert all. But locking: lock coord_lock once, lock each route row. Version checks per item. Weather check per item (forecast version must be current — same for all). Then insert all reviews. Single tx via withIdempotency wrapper (kind REVIEW_BATCH).

Occupation: 
```java
public MutationResponse createOccupation(OccupationCreateRequest request) {
    return withIdempotency(request.requestId(), KIND_OCCUPATION_CREATE, canonicalHash(request), () -> {
        ReviewPo review = reviewRepo.findReview(request.reviewId());
        if (review == null) → 404 REVIEW_NOT_FOUND
        if (!review.routeId().equals(request.routeId())) → 409 OCCUPATION_ROUTE_MISMATCH
        // lock route row + coord lock to get consistent current state
        long globalVersion = airspaceRepo.getGlobalVersionForUpdate();
        RoutePo route = routeRepo.findRouteForUpdate(request.routeId());
        boolean current = route != null && route.version() == review.routeVersion()
            && globalVersion == review.airspaceVersion()
            && weatherVersionsMatch(review);
        if (!"CLEAR".equals(review.conclusion())) → 409 OCCUPATION_NOT_CLEARED
        if (!current) → 409 REVIEW_STALE
        insert occupation with review's frozen versions
    });
}
```

getCurrentReview: current iff route matches && airspace matches && (review.forecastVersion == null || == current forecast) && (review.standardsVersion == null || == current standards).

Diagnostics: build VersionCheck list: routeVersion (reviewed vs current route version; route missing → current null, match false), airspaceVersion, forecastVersion (only if reviewed non-null), standardsVersion (only if reviewed non-null). stale = any mismatch. effectiveConclusion = stale ? "STALE" : conclusion.

